EPS THEY HAVE ALREADY FINISHED (they have these):\n- 01. The brief: Write down what you think it should do, before you read on.\n- 02. Session one \u2014 build it: Switch and magnet on the door frame, with your definition of one opening and your settle time. Sensor A inside, sensor B on the lead outside the door. Set a threshold on the count: after how many openings should it say something? Set a stop condition so it is not going off all evening. Set a sequence when it fires: ring, buzzer, lamp somewhere else in the house. Set the log running at an interval you choose.\n- 03. Card D1: Write on card D1 what one opening is. Write how many openings is too many. Write where the lamp goes.\n- 04. Session two \u2014 ask, then install: Show the machine working to whoever else uses that door. Ask permission before you mount anything. Switch on the frame, magnet on the door, lined up. Route the leads so the door can close without pinching them. Sensor B outside, under a porch. It must not get rained on. Open the door once and check the count goes up by exactly one.\n- 05. The week: Leave it completely alone. You get one change during the week. Write it down if you use it.\n- 06. Session three \u2014 read the week: Read the count and look at the log as a shape. Find which day was busiest. Find one moment you can name the cause of.\n\nCURRENT STEP 07 \u2014 Break it on purpose  (10 min)\nWhat this step is: Go and ask the household what annoyed them about it. Write down exactly what they say.\n\nWIRING FOR THE DOORKEEPER:\n- in: SENSOR A on A0 \u2014 reads warmth : the signal, the reading itself\n- in: SENSOR B on A1 \u2014 a metre away : the second reading, from somewhere else\n- in: SWITCH on SW \u2014 magnet near, or not : one event, or nothing\n- in: DIAL on DIAL \u2014 you turn it : every number you set\n- out: DISPLAY on DSP \u2014 shows it : the numbers, on their way to be shown\n- out: RING on RING \u2014 the verdict, in colour : the decision, seen across a room\n- out: